{%- comment -%}
  SHUDHI — Signature Product

  The homepage's product moment: a centred section header, an illustrated soap
  still-life on the left signed with the "generations" seal, and a benefits column
  on the right that ends in a Shop / Learn CTA pair. Sits directly under the hero.

  The left column used to be a packshot — "Our collection.webp" in a 6:5 card. It
  is now snippets/sh-soap-plate.liquid, an inline SVG. That change removed the
  `image` setting from the schema below. A merchant who had picked a photo still
  has that value stored in settings_data.json, but nothing reads it any more and
  the picker is gone from the editor, so there is no way to tell from the UI that
  the value was ever set. If a photo is ever wanted back here, the branch has to
  be rebuilt — and it must NOT bring back the clip-path wipe with it; see note 3.

  Four things here are deliberate and easy to undo by accident:

  1. The seal is a SIBLING of the plate, not a child. snippets/sh-gen-seal.liquid
     documents why: it is absolutely positioned, and any ancestor carrying
     [data-reveal] holds `transform: translateY(26px)` until .is-in lands, which
     makes that ancestor the containing block and visibly re-anchors the seal
     mid-reveal. .sh-signature__media is positioned but never transformed, so it
     is the one safe parent. Moving the seal inside the plate reintroduces the bug.

     `transform` is not the only way to cause it. will-change, filter,
     backdrop-filter, perspective and contain:paint all establish a containing
     block for absolutely positioned descendants too, and all of them read as
     harmless performance tweaks. shudhi-home.css:2344 carries the full list.

  2. The seal is rendered from the shared snippet but REPAINTED for a light
     surface in shudhi-home.css §22. The snippet is the dark-hero variant: its
     ring, arc labels and number are all --sh-gold, which the snippet's own
     comment notes is only legible on dark green (1.95:1 on this cream).

  3. THE PLATE'S REVEAL FAILS OPEN, and that is the whole reason it is built the
     way it is. The photo's entrance rested at `clip-path: inset(0 0 100% 0)` —
     fully clipped — and only opened when shudhi-home.js added .is-in. Any failure
     between parse and the observer firing therefore left a permanently blank
     column, with nothing on screen to suggest anything was missing.

     The plate inverts it: its resting state is the finished state, and
     assets/sh-soap-plate.js opts INTO the entrance by adding .is-armed. Same
     gesture, but JS off, a 404, or a throw earlier in boot all land on a
     complete illustration. One residual hole remains — if shudhi-home.js throws
     BEFORE reveal(), the plate is armed and never gets .is-in — and that is the
     standing risk level of every [data-reveal] element in this theme, which
     shudhi-home.js:423 already orders reveal() early to limit. Named here so it
     reads as known rather than missed.

  4. Both CTAs require label AND url together, the same bargain
     sections/sh-story-split.liquid:91 makes. A labelled link with no destination
     used to fall back to href="#", and an empty fragment means "top of the
     document" — so a reader who reached this band and pressed it was thrown back
     to the hero with no announcement (WCAG 2.4.4). Hiding the link is the honest
     failure mode; a dead one is not.

  Heading levels assume an <h1> already exists above — sections/sh-hero-scroll.liquid:100
  renders one on the homepage. h2 (section) / h3 (product) / h4 (feature) follows
  it without a skip. If this section is ever used on a template with no hero,
  the outline needs revisiting.

  Feature blocks lay out row-major in a 2-column grid, so the order they are
  entered in is the order they read left-to-right, top-to-bottom. Unlike
  sections/sh-ritual-benefits.liquid there is no per-block `column` setting: that
  section reproduces a deliberately lopsided 3-left/2-right fan, this one is a
  plain balanced grid where DOM order is the whole story.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign s = section.settings -%}

<section class="sh sh-signature" id="signature-product"
         style="--sh-signature-bg:{{ s.bg }};">

  <div class="sh-wrap">

    <header class="sh-signature__head"{% if s.animate %} data-reveal{% endif %}>
      {%- if s.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <div class="sh-eyebrow">
          {{ s.eyebrow }} {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'leaf' %}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <h2 class="sh-signature__title sh-serif">{{ s.title }}</h2>

      <div class="sh-signature__divider" aria-hidden="true">
        <span></span>{% render 'sh-icon', name: 'leaf' %}<span></span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="sh-signature__grid">

      <div class="sh-signature__media">

        {%- comment -%} [data-reveal] lives on the plate, never on
            .sh-signature__media — see note 1. The plate reserves its own box with
            aspect-ratio in §25, before anything paints, so there is no load-time
            reflow to guard against the way the old <img> needed intrinsic
            width/height. Being vector, there is also no second request: the whole
            illustration arrives in the document.

            `uid` is required, not optional — note the parameter list at the top of
            the snippet, and (1) in its header for what happens without it. {%- endcomment -%}
        {% render 'sh-soap-plate',
           uid: section.id,
           animate: s.animate,
           motion: s.plate_motion,
           cursor: s.plate_cursor %}

        {%- comment -%} uid is required, not optional: SVG ids are document-global and
            sections/sh-our-story.liquid renders its own seal further down the same
            page. Two seals sharing a uid would both bend their labels along the
            FIRST one's arcs. `section` is out of scope inside a rendered snippet,
            so the caller has to pass it. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if s.seal_number != blank -%}
          {% render 'sh-gen-seal',
             uid: section.id,
             number: s.seal_number,
             text_top: s.seal_top,
             text_bottom: s.seal_bottom %}
        {%- endif -%}

      </div>

      <div class="sh-signature__content"{% if s.animate %} data-reveal{% endif %}>

        {%- if s.sub_eyebrow != blank -%}
          <div class="sh-eyebrow">{{ s.sub_eyebrow }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}

        <h3 class="sh-signature__name sh-serif">{{ s.product_name }}</h3>

        <div class="sh-signature__rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>

        {%- if s.body != blank -%}
          <p class="sh-signature__text">{{ s.body }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
          <div class="sh-signature__features">
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              <div class="sh-signature__feature" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <span class="sh-signature__feature-icon">
                  {% render 'sh-icon', name: block.settings.icon %}
                </span>
                <div>
                  <h4>{{ block.settings.title }}</h4>
                  <p>{{ block.settings.text }}</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="sh-signature__cta">
          {%- if s.shop_label != blank and s.shop_link != blank -%}
            <a class="sh-btn sh-btn--solid" href="{{ s.shop_link }}">
              {{ s.shop_label }} {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'arrow-right' %}
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if s.learn_label != blank and s.learn_link != blank -%}
            <a class="sh-btn sh-btn--ghost" href="{{ s.learn_link }}">{{ s.learn_label }}</a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} Section-scoped and deferred, the same shape sections/sh-contact.liquid:414
    uses, rather than a new global entry in layout/theme.liquid. Emitted only when
    there is actually a job to do: with both switches off the file does nothing but
    arm an element that has no entrance to run, so it is not worth the request.

    Note what does NOT depend on this file — all of the artwork, and all of the
    ambient motion, which is CSS. Losing this script costs the entrance and the
    cursor parallax. Nothing else. See note 3. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- if s.animate or s.plate_cursor -%}
  <script src="{{ 'sh-soap-plate.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "SH · Signature Product",
  "class": "index-section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Section header" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Our Signature" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Heading", "default": "One Soap. Countless Benefits." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Product" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "sub_eyebrow", "label": "Content eyebrow", "default": "Our Signature Soap" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "product_name", "label": "Product name", "default": "Shudhi Herbals Soap" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Body text", "default": "A handcrafted herbal soap made with time-honored Ayurvedic ingredients to gently cleanse, nourish, and balance your skin and aura. Free from harsh chemicals, full of nature's goodness." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Illustration" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "The left column is a drawn soap still-life, not a photograph, so there is nothing to upload here." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "plate_motion", "label": "Ambient motion", "default": true,
      "info": "The slow drift of the leaves, particles and light. Separate from \"Animate on scroll\" below, which controls the entrance only." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "plate_cursor", "label": "Follow cursor", "default": true,
      "info": "Desktop pointers only. Ignored on touch devices and for visitors who have asked for reduced motion." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Seal" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "seal_number", "label": "Seal number", "default": "4",
      "info": "Leave empty to hide the seal entirely." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "seal_top", "label": "Seal text — top arc", "default": "Inspired by" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "seal_bottom", "label": "Seal text — bottom arc", "default": "Generations of herbal wisdom",
      "info": "Roughly 28 characters fit on each arc at this size — longer runs off the end of the semicircle." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Buttons" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Each button needs its label and its link set together — neither renders on its own." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "shop_label", "label": "Primary button label", "default": "Shop Now" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "shop_link", "label": "Primary button link" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "learn_label", "label": "Secondary link label", "default": "Learn More" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "learn_link", "label": "Secondary link URL" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Appearance" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "animate", "label": "Animate on scroll", "default": true },
    { "type": "color", "id": "bg", "label": "Background", "default": "#f6ede1",
      "info": "Keep it light — the heading, body, seal and divider colours are tuned for a light surface, and the illustration's warm ivory is tuned against this value." }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "feature", "name": "Feature", "settings": [
      { "type": "select", "id": "icon", "label": "Icon", "default": "leaf", "options": [
        { "value": "leaf", "label": "Leaf" }, { "value": "lotus", "label": "Lotus" },
        { "value": "drop", "label": "Drop" }, { "value": "plant", "label": "Plant" },
        { "value": "sparkle", "label": "Sparkle" }, { "value": "heart", "label": "Heart" },
        { "value": "hand", "label": "Hand" }, { "value": "mortar", "label": "Mortar" } ] },
      { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Title", "default": "Cleanses Deeply" },
      { "type": "textarea", "id": "text", "label": "Description", "default": "Removes impurities without stripping natural moisture." }
    ] }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 6,
  "presets": [ { "name": "SH · Signature Product", "blocks": [
    { "type": "feature", "settings": { "icon": "leaf",    "title": "Cleanses Deeply",  "text": "Removes impurities without stripping natural moisture." } },
    { "type": "feature", "settings": { "icon": "sparkle", "title": "Gentle & Safe",    "text": "Suitable for all skin types, including sensitive skin." } },
    { "type": "feature", "settings": { "icon": "drop",    "title": "Nourishes Skin",   "text": "Herbal ingredients restore and maintain skin health." } },
    { "type": "feature", "settings": { "icon": "mortar",  "title": "Ayurvedic Care",   "text": "Ancient herbs known for their therapeutic benefits." } },
    { "type": "feature", "settings": { "icon": "lotus",   "title": "Balances Aura",    "text": "Purifies your energy and uplifts your mood." } },
    { "type": "feature", "settings": { "icon": "heart",   "title": "Mindful Ritual",   "text": "Transforms everyday showers into moments of self-care." } }
  ] } ]
}
{% endschema %}
